q:
A circle of radius $3$ is inscribed in a trapezoid $ABCD$ with $AD\parallel BC$ and with angles $B$ and $C$ acute. If $AB=7$ and $CD=8$, find the area of trapezoid $ABCD$.

Here $XY$ denotes the length of segment $XY$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(245);
real left=sqrt(13),right=sqrt(28),bottom=(15+left+right)/2;
pair B=(0,0),C=(bottom,0),A=(left,6),D=(bottom-right,6);
pair I=((7+left)/2,3),T=I+3*dir(-30);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);draw(circle(I,3));dot(I);
draw(I--T);label("3",(I+T)/2,NE);
label("A",A,NW);label("B",B,SW);label("C",C,SE);label("D",D,NE);
label("7",(A+B)/2,W);label("8",(C+D)/2,E);
[/asy]

There are cells $A,B,C,D,E,F$ at the vertices of a regular hexagon. From each cell, a move may be made to either of the cells at adjacent vertices or to the cell at the opposite vertex. How many routes start at cell $A$, visit every other cell exactly once without visiting $A$ along the way, and return to $A$?

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(215);
pair[] V;
string[] names={"A","B","C","D","E","F"};
for(int i=0;i<6;++i) V.push(2*dir(90+60*i));
for(int i=0;i<6;++i) draw(V[i]--V[(i+1)%6]);
for(int i=0;i<3;++i) draw(V[i]--V[i+3]);
for(int i=0;i<6;++i) { filldraw(circle(V[i],0.32),white,black);label(names[i],V[i]); }
[/asy]

There are $36$ equilateral triangular tiles of side length $1$, assembled to form the board shown in the figure. Call the $30$ points marked by black dots good points.

How many ways are there to color each tile on this board either red or blue so that the following condition holds?

At every good point, among the tiles having that point as a vertex, the number colored red equals the number colored blue.

Colorings that coincide after rotating or reflecting the board are counted as different.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(265);
pair[] nodes,edgeA,edgeB;
int[] counts;
void addNode(pair p) {
  for(pair q:nodes) if(abs(p-q)<0.00001) return;
  nodes.push(p);
}
void addEdge(pair a,pair b) {
  for(int i=0;i<edgeA.length;++i)
    if((abs(a-edgeA[i])<0.00001 && abs(b-edgeB[i])<0.00001) ||
       (abs(a-edgeB[i])<0.00001 && abs(b-edgeA[i])<0.00001)) { ++counts[i];return; }
  edgeA.push(a);edgeB.push(b);counts.push(1);
}
for(int k=0;k<6;++k) {
  pair c=sqrt(3)*dir(30+60*k);addNode(c);
  pair[] vertices;
  for(int j=0;j<6;++j) { pair p=c+dir(60*j);vertices.push(p);addNode(p);draw(c--p,gray(0.45)+dashed+linewidth(0.45)); }
  for(int j=0;j<6;++j) addEdge(vertices[j],vertices[(j+1)%6]);
}
for(int i=0;i<edgeA.length;++i) {
  pen p=counts[i]==1 ? black+linewidth(0.8) : gray(0.45)+dashed+linewidth(0.45);
  draw(edgeA[i]--edgeB[i],p);
}
for(pair p:nodes) fill(circle(p,0.075),black);
[/asy]
